---
import DesktopLayout from '../layouts/DesktopLayout.astro';
import Window from '../components/Window.astro';
import '../styles/menubar.css';
---
<DesktopLayout title="Privacy Policy — Real Serious Business">
  <Window
    title="Privacy Policy - Notepad"
    icon="/icons/win98/notepad_file.ico"
    path="/privacy"
    backHref="/"
    defaultWidth={580}
    defaultHeight={520}
    defaultX={100}
    defaultY={50}
    noBodyScroll={true}
  >
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;height:100%;">
      <div class="win-menubar">
        <button class="win-menubar-btn">File</button>
        <button class="win-menubar-btn">Edit</button>
        <button class="win-menubar-btn">Search</button>
        <button class="win-menubar-btn">Help</button>
      </div>
      <div class="notepad-body">Privacy Policy
Last updated: November 2026
----------------------------------------

OVERVIEW
----------------------------------------

Real Serious Business is a personal blog. This
policy describes what little data is handled
when you visit this site.

DATA COLLECTION
----------------------------------------

This site uses Kit (kit.com) for email
newsletter subscriptions. When you subscribe,
Kit collects your email address and may collect
additional information you voluntarily provide.
Kit processes this data according to their own
privacy policy (https://kit.com/privacy).

You can unsubscribe at any time using the link
included in every email.

Beyond the newsletter and the shared desktop
features described below (live cursors, chat
and guestbook), this site does not collect,
store, or process any other personal data on
a server.

  - No cookies from this site

ANALYTICS
----------------------------------------

This site uses PostHog for anonymous usage
analytics (page views, basic interactions).
No personally identifiable information is
collected. See PostHog's privacy policy at
https://posthog.com/privacy for details.

LIVE CURSORS, CHAT AND GUESTBOOK
----------------------------------------

While you have the site open, your browser
stays connected to a server (a Cloudflare
Worker) so visitors can see each other.

  - Other visitors online at the same time see
    your mouse pointer moving on the desktop,
    with your nickname next to it. Nicknames
    start as a random "GuestNNNN" and you can
    change them in Chat.
  - Cursor positions and who is online are not
    saved; they disappear when you leave.
  - Chat messages are shown to everyone online.
    The latest 100 are kept so newcomers can
    see recent conversation.
  - Guestbook entries (the name and message you
    type) are public and kept until removed.
  - A total visit count is kept. It is only a
    number and says nothing about who visited.

Please don't post personal information in the
chat or guestbook. Messages and entries can be
removed by the site owner; ask via the contact
details on this site if you want yours taken
down.

To stop spam, a scrambled one-way hash of your
IP address (not the address itself) is used to
limit guestbook signing to once every 10
minutes. It is deleted after those 10 minutes.

LOCAL STORAGE
----------------------------------------

Your browser's localStorage is used to remember
window positions, font preferences, your chat
nickname, and Minesweeper settings and best
times. This data stays on your device, except
that your nickname is shown to others when you
are online (see above).

THIRD-PARTY LINKS
----------------------------------------

Posts may link to external websites. This site
has no control over and assumes no
responsibility for the content or privacy
practices of any third-party sites.

CLOUDFLARE
----------------------------------------

This site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages.
Cloudflare may log basic request metadata
(IP address, user agent) as part of its
infrastructure. See Cloudflare's privacy
policy for details.

CONTACT
----------------------------------------

If you have any questions about this policy,
you can reach out via the contact information
listed on this site.

----------------------------------------
      </div>
    </div>
  </Window>
</DesktopLayout>
